-- 181_native_render_increment1.surql -- Option A INCREMENT 1 PASSED: the game's own D3D11 bring-up
-- (FUN_1402B22D0 -> FUN_1402B80F0) runs inside the SUPERGUN runner on the runner's own window and
-- creates the game's own device / immediate context / swapchain. 2026-09-05.
-- Forward slashes only in ref/note strings.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:supergun_native_render_inc1_20260905 SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='sg_runner.exe --pre d3dcap/ttd/runs/vs-01/pre --arc <INFLATED AFS> --out C:/Users/trist/AppData/Local/Temp/sg_native1 --gs exe --no-flush --heaps --host-gfx --noop-import 1408db190,1408db108 --native-render --dlist-window 120 (supergun/supersoaker/runner/sg_runner/src/native.rs). Decompiles: FUN_1402B22D0, FUN_1402B80F0, FUN_1402B2250, FUN_1402693D0, FUN_1403382E0, FUN_14011F340/F310, FUN_14011EA90, FUN_14026F0E0, FUN_14026CC10/CC40/CD40, FUN_14012D120/D3A0/D230/D2D0, FUN_140042B80, FUN_1407FD5DE, FUN_140371300/12B0/13D0/1880/1830/1950, FUN_140396AE0, FUN_1402B34A0, FUN_1402B3C60, FUN_140130730. IAT names from the runner same-boot export map (iat_map.txt).',
  note='runner.log: 15 native-render IAT slots (13 un-trapped to the real export + CreateThread/ResumeThread stubbed), heaps 15/64; GATE 1 PASSED: device +0xB8, context +0xC0, swapchain +0x892EA8, entry HWND == ours, displays 1, feature code +0x50 = 5 (11.0), client 1280x720, MT +0x42 = 0, CreateThread calls 1, *0x142EBD8F0 == new object; 120 ticks clock 281 -> 401, traps hit 0, EXIT 0.';

UPSERT finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-05',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='INCREMENT 1 PASSED: the game constructs its own nDraw (device + context + swapchain) on the SUPERGUN window when FUN_1402B22D0 is called with FUN_1402B2250 exact arguments',
  statement='Recipe, all constants from the decompiles: nDraw = zeroed 0x892F30 (FUN_1402B2250 alloc(0x892F30, 0x10)); app object = zeroed 0x2000 with +0x148 = our HWND, +0x150 = 0, stored at DAT_142EBCD00 (FUN_14026CD40 writes +0x178+n*8 n<0x100 and count +0x978; FUN_14026F0E0 writes +0x97C+i*0x200 i<8 -- 0x2000 covers every write); DAT_142EBC8B8 = zeroed 0x40000 (FUN_1402B80F0 reads +0x3FE58 as MSAA count; <2 => single-threaded); DAT_142EBD930 = 1 and DAT_142EBD938/940/948/950/958 = 0 (skip d3d9 load; 938/940 are CALLED if non-null and held the capture session d3d9 addresses); config object 0x140A5CA30: +0x8 ini path was a dead heap pointer -> 0, string allocator *0x140A5C770 was host -> in-image Default heap 0x142E12EF0; nDraw+0x87AB98 = a valid char* because FUN_14026F0E0 strncpy-s from param_1[0x10F573] for mask entries with bits 0x2|0x8 and the DAT_14092C1D8 table is [1,2,8,10,20,4,40,80]; then FUN_1402B22D0(nDraw, 2, 0x200000, 0x200000, 0x400000, 0x100000, 2, 0, 0x23E). IAT: real exports for 0x1408DB0F8 CreateEventA, DB100 RtlInitializeCriticalSection, DB1D8/DB1E0 QueryPerformanceFrequency/Counter, DB1F0 LoadLibraryA, DB328 GetPrivateProfileStringA, DB428 FreeLibrary, DB430 GetProcAddress, DB438 WideCharToMultiByte, DB6B0 GetWindowRect, DB728 GetClientRect, DB750 SetForegroundWindow, DB838 D3D11CreateDeviceAndSwapChain (FUN_1407FD5DE is jmp [0x1408DB838]; MEASURED: GetProcAddress(d3d11, D3D11CreateDeviceAndSwapChain) == the dump slot value 0x7FFCCFF72470); DB3C0 CreateThread and DB3D0 ResumeThread stubbed (RenderingThread FUN_1402B9780 never started). Gate corrections vs seed 180: the immediate context is nDraw+0xC0 (not +0xC8: D3D11CreateDeviceAndSwapChain(.., &scdesc, +0xC8 swapchain, +0xB8 device, &fl, +0xC0 context), then +0xC8 moves to display entry 0 at +0x892EA8 and is cleared). Display entry stride 0x30: +0x892E98 HWND, +0x892EA0 IDXGIOutput, +0x892EA8 IDXGISwapChain; +0x892EF8 display count; +0x50 feature-level code (5 = 11.0); +0xE0/+0xE4 client size. Swapchain desc: R8G8B8A8_UNORM (0x1C), 60/1, 1 sample, RENDER_TARGET_OUTPUT, BufferCount 1, windowed, DISCARD -- blt model, so the runner opens a window WITHOUT its own swapchain (gfx::open_window).',
  consequence='Option A is no longer blocked on graphics init: *0x142EBD8F0 is a LIVE nDraw with a live device, and the ring executor state slots are populated by the game own constructor path. Increment 2 = per frame encode FUN_14006F5E0 -> FUN_140070940 (gate *(config+0x774)) + submit FUN_1402BCC60 -> FUN_1402B6F30 + present FUN_1402B6A50, then the pixel gate docs/RENDER-PIXEL-GATE.md.',
  caveat='Increment 1 draws nothing. --host-gfx is still on for the LOAD path (staging trio at host_device+0xDBD08, FUN_140272700 -> rr_tex_map, band ret-stubs); increment 2 must retire those so the game own texture create/map/upload run against the live device. The FreeLibrary(d3d11) at the end of FUN_1402B80F0 is balanced by the runner own LoadLibraryA(d3d11.dll) done for name resolution, which keeps the DLL pinned.';

RELATE finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed->cites->source:supergun_native_render_inc1_20260905 SET id='e181_inc1_src';
RELATE finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed->cites->finding:native_render_bringup_path SET id='e181_inc1_prior';
RELATE finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed->cites->finding:native_render_state_is_lookup_not_lazy SET id='e181_inc1_lookup';

UPDATE finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed SET status='confirmed';
UPDATE finding:native_render_bringup_path SET caveat='RESOLVED 2026-09-05 by finding:native_render_inc1_bringup_passed: the swapchain sits at display entry 0 +0x892EA8 (entry stride 0x30: +0x892E98 HWND, +0x892EA0 output), the immediate context at +0xC0. DAT_142EBCD00 and PTR_PTR_140A5CA30 did NOT need the app init subtree: a zeroed 0x2000 app object with +0x148 = HWND and the in-image config object with its dead heap pointers nulled suffice. Gate: docs/RENDER-PIXEL-GATE.md.';
